1. DEFINITIONS

"Runner" means the compiled Bitbybit Runner JavaScript bundle files
(bitbybit-runner-babylonjs.js, bitbybit-runner-viewer-babylonjs.js,
bitbybit-runner-threejs.js, bitbybit-runner-playcanvas.js,
bitbybit-runner-core.js, and their respective "lite" variants), the
associated Web Worker files, WebAssembly binaries, and any supporting
assets distributed alongside them, except the Bitbybit OCCT Kernel and the
license files served beside it.

"Bitbybit OCCT Kernel" means Open CASCADE Technology (OCCT) compiled
together with the Bitbybit kernel layer, in each of its builds: the
WebAssembly files bitbybit-dev-occt*.wasm the Runner loads. It does not
include the Manifold or JSCAD kernels, which are separate open-source
projects under their own licenses. It is licensed under the MIT License (see
section 4).

"Open-Source Components" means the portions of the Runner derived from
third-party open-source projects, as listed in the NOTICE file. These
components are governed by their respective licenses.

"Proprietary Components" means all portions of the Runner that are not
Open-Source Components, including but not limited to proprietary algorithms,
orchestration logic, and integration code authored by MB "Bit by bit
developers".

"CDN Assets" means the Runner files and supporting assets (Web Workers,
WebAssembly binaries, fonts) hosted on the Bitbybit CDN at
git-cdn.bitbybit.dev or any successor URL.

